// expect: refuse E_ConstructorArity
// `Pair` holds two fields and the pattern names one, so the arm takes apart
// a shape the type does not have. Every error refuses the executable. Until
// 2026-10-16 this class reported and the program compiled anyway: on boot
// 969f2559 it answered 7, the first field, as though the pattern were whole.
type Pair = Pair(Int, Int)

fn first(p) = match p {
  Pair(a) => a,
}

fn main() = first(Pair(7, 8))
